6. In .LLMDD/tools/run-waves.py replace the whole ModelFallbackChain class (old lines 203-218) with the exact frozen slotted dataclass below (same iteration, len, and repr behavior; chain is now a tuple): ```python
@dataclass(slots=True, frozen=True)
class ModelFallbackChain:
    """Manages fallback order for model attempts."""
    primary_model: str
    fallback_models: Sequence[str] = ()
    chain: Sequence[str] = ()

    def __post_init__(self) -> None:
        merged: list[str] = [self.primary_model, *self.fallback_models]
        object.__setattr__(self, "chain", tuple(merged))

    def __iter__(self) -> Iterator[str]:
        return iter(self.chain)

    def __len__(self) -> int:
        return len(self.chain)

    def __repr__(self) -> str:
        return " u2192 ".join(self.chain)
``` Callers keep passing a list (parse_args yields a list); convert at the single construction site inside run_wave_parallel (cu-003 converts that call to `ModelFallbackChain(coder_model, tuple(coder_fallbacks))`). Prove: `python3 -m py_compile .LLMDD/tools/run-waves.py` prints nothing and exits 0.
